pvai (0.5.15-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Confirmed delivery: pvai run pastes a prompt only into a free prompt
    box and presses Return only once the box shows it. A prompt that did
    not go in, or got no UserPromptSubmit in time, goes back to the front
    of the queue, and the session waits on a "screen" dialog showing the
    screen. accepted says queued, the new delivered message follows once
    Claude Code has the prompt. answer send types without the check.
  * A slash command's picker that closes after its output is in the
    transcript leaves the session idle, not busy.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:20:00 +0100

pvai (0.5.14-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * A Claude Code started from a shell command of a session inherits
    pvai's environment; its hooks and status line no longer take over that
    session (claudeSession, transcript, state, usage). Another session id
    counts only before the first, while starting, or with SessionStart
    after /clear, /resume or a compaction.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0100

pvai (0.5.13-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Dialogs no hook reports (pickers, notices to confirm such as "Teach
    auto mode about your environment?") are read off the terminal: pvai
    run keeps a model of the screen, the session is waiting with dialog
    "screen" and the dialog's text in dialogInfo.text, prompts stay
    queued instead of being typed into it.
  * answer: choice key:up|down|left|right|enter|esc|tab|space or a digit or
    letter sends one key into a dialog; allow/deny are Return/Esc for a
    screen dialog.

